    "response": " To find the average speed of the car over the interval \\(0 \\leq t \\leq 10\\) seconds, we use the formula for the average value of a function:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average speed} = \\frac{1}{b-a} \\int_a^b v(t) \\, dt\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(a = 0\\), \\(b = 10\\), and \\(v(t) = 3t - \\frac{t^2}{2}\\). Plugging in these values, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average speed} = \\frac{1}{10-0} \\int_0^{10} \\left(3t - \\frac{t^2}{2}\\right) \\, dt = \\frac{1}{10} \\int_0^{10} \\left(3t - \\frac{t^2}{2}\\right) \\, dt\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to evaluate the integral. We do this by integrating each term separately:\n\n\\[\n\\int_0^{10} \\left(3t - \\frac{t^2}{2}\\right) \\, dt = \\int_0^{10} 3t \\, dt - \\int_0^{10} \\frac{t^2}{2} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nThe integral of \\(3t\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\int_0^{10} 3t \\, dt = 3 \\left[ \\frac{t^2}{2} \\right]_0^{10} = 3 \\left( \\frac{10^2}{2} - \\frac{0^2}{2} \\right) = 3 \\left( \\frac{100}{2} \\right",
